q: table.c -- a times table
spec: Print a 5 by 5 multiplication table: five rows, row r holding r*1 to
spec: r*5, every number printed with `%4d` (right-aligned in four columns),
spec: no spaces added, a newline after each row. The first row is
spec: `   1   2   3   4   5`.
file: table.c
prog: #include <stdio.h>
prog: 
prog: int main(void)
prog: {
prog: 	for (int row = 1; row <= 5; row++) {
prog: 		for (int col = 1; col <= 5; col++)
prog: 			printf("%4d", row * col);
prog: 		printf("\n");
prog: 	}
prog: 	return 0;
prog: }
case: table
case: table | tail -n 1
case: table | head -n 2
hint: one loop inside another; the newline belongs after the inner loop, not inside it
